@startuml float-nan-two-relations
' CBR-L09 — why float NaN needs TWO relations, and what happens if they are conflated.
' Colour key:
'   blue   = the NUMERIC PREDICATE lane (Rholang's comparison operators, IEEE 754 §5.11)
'   green  = the STRUCTURAL IDENTITY lane (term equality: matcher, containers, hashing)
'   amber  = the shared carrier the two lanes read
'   red    = the MEASURED failure produced by conflating them
'   grey   = withdrawn / historical state

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam RectangleBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #F9A825

title <b>CBR-L09 — one carrier, two relations: why the split is correct and not a compromise</b>\n<size:11>Conflating them does not merely mis-answer a comparison; it stops the rewrite engine terminating.</size>

rectangle "**The float carrier**\n<i>CanonicalFloat64</i>  (<i>runtime/src/canonical_float.rs</i>)\n<size:10>reflexive <i>PartialEq</i>; <i>Ord</i> sorts NaN LAST; <latex>-0.0 \mapsto +0.0</latex> at parse</size>" as CARRIER #FFE0B2

package "Lane N — **NUMERIC PREDICATE**\n<size:10>\"how do these two numbers compare?\"</size>" as LANEN #E3F2FD {
  rectangle "Rholang's six comparison arms\n<i>Eq  Ne  Gt  Lt  GtEq  LtEq</i>\n<size:10><i>languages/src/rholang.rs</i> @ <i>19510082</i>\n:1499 :1566 :1626 :1677 :1728 :1779</size>" as ARMS #BBDEFB
  rectangle "**IEEE 754 §5.11**\n<size:10>a NaN is <b>UNORDERED</b>:</size>\n<latex>\mathrm{NaN} = \mathrm{NaN} \;\Rightarrow\; \mathtt{false}</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{NaN} \neq \mathrm{NaN} \;\Rightarrow\; \mathtt{true}</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{NaN} > x \;\Rightarrow\; \mathtt{false}</latex>" as IEEE #90CAF9
  ARMS -down-> IEEE : reaches PAST the carrier\nwith **.get()**
}

package "Lane S — **STRUCTURAL IDENTITY**\n<size:10>\"are these the same term?\"</size>" as LANES #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle "the spatial matcher · a term-keyed <i>Map</i>\n<i>HashSet</i> membership · <i>Proc::semantic_hash</i>\nDovetail **saturation**" as CONSUMERS #C8E6C9
  rectangle "must be an **EQUIVALENCE RELATION**\n<latex>\forall t:\; t \sim t</latex>  (reflexive)\n<latex>t \sim u \Rightarrow u \sim t</latex>  (symmetric)\n<latex>t \sim u \wedge u \sim v \Rightarrow t \sim v</latex>" as EQUIV #A5D6A7
  CONSUMERS -down-> EQUIV : requires
}

CARRIER -down-> ARMS
CARRIER -down-> CONSUMERS : **UNCHANGED**\nby the ruling

note right of IEEE #E1F5FE
  <b>Rust's native f64 comparison is ALREADY IEEE</b>, so
  <i>x.get() > y.get()</i> is correct by construction — no
  special-casing. ⓘ Upstream needs an explicit NaN branch
  (<i>reduce.rs:3146-3162</i>) only because it routes through
  <i>partial_cmp</i>, whose <i>None</i> it would map to "equal".
end note

note right of EQUIV #E8F5E9
  <b>Upstream has the SAME split.</b>
  <i>RhoTypes.proto:269</i> stores <i>g_double</i> as
  <b>raw bits</b>, so prost-derived <i>PartialEq</i>
  compares BIT PATTERNS — two same-bit NaNs are
  structurally equal upstream too.
end note

rectangle "⚠⚠ **CONFLATE THEM** — make the CARRIER follow IEEE\n<size:10>patch <i>CanonicalFloat64::PartialEq</i> to <i>self.0 == other.0</i></size>" as CONFLATE #FFCDD2
rectangle "**MEASURED FAILURE**, not a hypothesis\n<size:11><i>saturation for language Rholang stopped before\nconvergence: IterationLimit</i></size>\n<size:10>on the FIRST fold of <i>0.0 / 0.0</i></size>" as BOOM #EF9A9A
rectangle "**Why:** saturation recognises a fixpoint by\ncomparing terms. IEEE equality is deliberately\n<b>IRREFLEXIVE</b> on NaN —\n<latex>\mathrm{NaN} \neq \mathrm{NaN}</latex>\n— so a term is never equal to itself and can\n<b>never be recognised as unchanged</b>." as WHY #FFCDD2

EQUIV -right[#C62828,thickness=2]-> CONFLATE : the tempting\n"consistency" fix
CONFLATE -down[#C62828,thickness=2]-> BOOM
BOOM -down[#C62828,thickness=2]-> WHY

rectangle "**WITHDRAWN 2026-07-29** — the arithmetic refusal\n<size:10>every float arm answered the <i>error</i> term where IEEE defines a value;\n<latex>\div</latex> by <i>b77e657c</i>, then <latex>+\;-\;\times</latex> and unary <latex>-</latex> by <i>ab885336</i></size>" as OLD #ECEFF1
OLD -up[#78909C,dashed]-> CARRIER : made NaN **REACHABLE**,\nwhich is what made Lane N\nobservable at all

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#BBDEFB> blue   | Lane N — the numeric predicate; IEEE 754 §5.11 governs |
  |<#C8E6C9> green  | Lane S — structural identity; must be an equivalence relation |
  |<#FFE0B2> amber  | the shared carrier both lanes read; **unchanged** by the ruling |
  |<#FFCDD2> red    | the measured consequence of conflating the two lanes |
  |<#ECEFF1> grey   | withdrawn / historical state |
end legend

@enduml
